      "role": "user",
      "content": "the drift is what's bothering me though. it’s not just random noise, it's increasing in a way that feels almost intentional, like a header or a checksum in a data packet. if you look at the delta between the drifts themselves, it's not linear. \n\nif this wasn't just a satellite doing its job, but instead was using these windows to transmit something encrypted via signal timing... what kind of structure would you expect to see in those micro-delays? would they follow a known protocol or something more custom?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
