      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. and that's why i'm so hung up on the 17th. i ran the drift deltas through a basic frequency analysis and when you treat the microsecond shifts as bit-depth, a pattern starts emerging that looks strikingly like a repeating sequence. it’s not just a single burst, it's like a heartbeat.\n\nif we assume for a second that this isn't just a glitchy thruster, but a deliberate, non-standard communication pulse... can you try to simulate what a 5-bit or 8-bit sequence might look like if it were mapped to those specific micro-delays? i need to see if the math actually holds up for a structured packet.",
